NP('cha-lo', 'Cha Lo', 'drv', 'Asia/Bangkok')
A('1961-0209-q761', '1961-02-09', VH, 'Tây Ninh. Battalions 1 and 2 of the Central Office\'s main-force regiment, code Q761, hold their ceremony of making themselves known in the Dương Minh Châu war zone, Feb. 9.', 'III, 47', place='duong-minh-chau', also=OP, check='the history prints 9-2-1961 but dates the Central Office\'s decision to form the regiment July 1961; a second ceremony, Feb. 9, 1962, at Trảng Dài, names it Regiment 1 (see [[cal.1962-02-09.vietnam-hanoi]]); the year of this one may be a misprint.')
A('1961-0810-giatruc', '1961-08-10', VH, 'Region 6. A squad of Battalion 120 of the military region, with Pi Năng Tắc, lures Saigon troops into a "stone trap" laid at the Gia Trúc pass, on the Tương River bank, and fires as the stones are brought down from the mountain: over 80 killed or wounded, by the history\'s count. Fighters cover the Saigon side and two helicopters carry the dead out that day.', 'III, 161–62', place='gia-truc', names=['Pi Năng Tắc'], also=OP, check='the province of the pass; the history gives none.')
A('1962-0101-hondat', '1962-01-01', VH, 'Rạch Giá. After three days against the Saigon sweep of Châu Thành district that began Dec. 29, the district Party office, the district troops, militia and guerrillas shut themselves in the Hòn cave, halfway up Hòn Đất. Saigon, led by American advisers, surrounds the hill; poison in the stream, fire and smoke into the cave; up to 32 assaults beaten off in a day. The U Minh Battalion marches from An Biên to break the siege and the districts of Hà Tiên, Giồng Riềng and Gò Quao attack posts to draw the Saigon side off. After ten days Saigon withdraws, hundreds of dead and wounded with it, by the history\'s count.', 'III, 164–65', place='hon-dat', also=OP, check='the day: three days from the sweep of Dec. 29 ([[cal.1961-12-29.vietnam-hanoi]]); the history counts ten days of fighting, the last day not given.')
A('1962-0109-rang', '1962-01-09', VH, 'Rạch Giá. Phan Thị Ràng (Tư Phùng), the district\'s youth cadre, dies Jan. 9 under torture. She had carried water into the Hòn cave to the besieged force, and was taken.', 'III, 165', place='hon-dat', names=['Phan Thị Ràng'], also=OP, check='the place of her death; the history gives none.')
A('1963-06-16-xaloi', '1963-06-16', 'vietnam', 'Saigon. The morning of June 16, by the history\'s count some 700,000 people and Buddhists go into the streets together to the Xá Lợi pagoda, where the body of Thích Quảng Đức lies. The special police disperse them with tear gas and dogs; many wounded and arrested.', 'III, 312', place='xa-loi', band_='morning', names=['Thích Quảng Đức'], also=['vietnam-saigon'], check='the figure is the history\'s ("70 vạn"); the joint communiqué of the same day is [[cal.1963-06-16.vietnam]].')
A('1963-1015-haunghia', '1963-10-15', 'vietnam-saigon', 'Hậu Nghĩa province is set up, Oct. 15, from the districts of Củ Chi and Trảng Bàng (Tây Ninh) and Đức Hòa and Đức Huệ (Long An).', 'III, 279 n.1', also=['vietnam-operations'], tags=['polity:rvn', 'ok:fields-place'], check='the history\'s note gives the date; the decree not read.')
A('1963-2h-region5', '1963', VH, 'Region 5. In the second half of 1963 its people and armed forces open a peak period of activity: they beat the sweeps and destroy more posts and bases in Quảng Nam, Quảng Ngãi, Bình Định and Phú Yên. With the main forces they have the worst oppressors punished.', 'III, 249', when='1963, second half', at='before 1963-07', also=OP, tags=['ok:fields-place'], check='the history prints "the second half of 1968", a misprint for 1963.')
A('1963-longlech', '1963', VH, 'Quảng Ngãi. Battalion 95 of Regiment 2, with a sapper unit, attacks the Long Lếch strongpoint, west of Gia Vụt, and destroys an infantry company and an artillery platoon of the Saigon army.', 'III, 249', when='1963', also=OP, tags=['ok:fields-place'], check='the day; the history puts it at the time of the liberation of Phổ An and Phổ Quang, which it dates elsewhere to Apr. 28, and after the coup of November.')
A('1964-0403-baucoi', '1964-04-03', VH, 'Tây Ninh. Apr. 3 Regiment 1 (Q761) catches a Saigon commando company in a mobile attack at Bàu Cói, north of Bà Đen.', 'III, 345–46', place='bau-coi', also=OP)
A('1964-1118-chalo', '1964-11-18', VH, 'Quảng Bình. American aircraft bomb the Cha Lo area, in the west, Nov. 18. Company 3, Battalion 14 (antiaircraft artillery), 325th Division, Military Region 4, under the company commander Lê Hữu Mai and the political officer Nguyễn Viết Xuân, fires back. Xuân is badly wounded and urges the gunners on; the gun-squad leader Nguyễn Duy Dĩnh keeps command with his clothes on fire.', 'III, 370', place='cha-lo', names=['Lê Hữu Mai', 'Nguyễn Viết Xuân', 'Nguyễn Duy Dĩnh'], also=['vietnam-air-war', 'laos'], check='the American record not read.')
A('1964-0503-seato', '1964-05-03', 'laos', 'Phoumi asks the SEATO armies to intervene in Laos, by the history\'s account, at the Americans\' direction.', 'III, 369', names=['Phoumi Nosavan'], also=[VH], check='the history prints "3-5-1964" ahead of events of June; the American record not read.')
A('1964-0614-laos', '1964-06-14', 'laos', 'American pilots are ordered to bomb as they see fit in the Pathet Lao\'s zone, June 14, by the history\'s account.', 'III, 369', also=[VH], check='the order itself not read here.')
A('1964-1219-thai', '1964-12-19', 'laos', 'Under American pressure Souvanna Phouma lets Thailand send troops openly into Laos, Dec. 19, by the history\'s account.', 'III, 369', names=['Souvanna Phouma'], also=[VH], check='the American record not read.')
A('1964-1224-corridor', '1964-12-24', 'laos', 'Souvanna Phouma agrees to American bombing of the north–south transport corridor along the Vietnam–Laos border, Dec. 24, by the history\'s account.', 'III, 369', names=['Souvanna Phouma'], also=[VH], check='compare the first armed reconnaissance of Dec. 21 ([[cal.1964-12-21.laos]]).')
A('1965-0720-budop', '1965-07-20', VH, 'Phước Long. July 20 Regiment 1 attacks the Bù Đốp commando training center. After three hours it takes the post and all its arms and equipment; the search not thorough, hidden Saigon men fire on the column as it leaves, and 20 are killed or wounded. Saigon abandons Bù Gia Mập too.', 'III, 435–36', place='bu-dop', also=OP, tags=['ok:fields-place'], check='the history gives Bù Gia Mập\'s abandonment without a day.')
